---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Style Guide · Hand Notes"
  description="Design system for Hand Notes — colors, typography, components, and patterns."
>

<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="cover">
    <div class="cover-subject">Hand Notes · Design System</div>
    <h1>Style <span>Guide</span></h1>
    <div class="cover-sub">Colors, typography, components &amp; patterns</div>
    <div class="cover-doodle">🎨</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Colors ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page blue-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">🎨</span>
      <span class="section-title">Color Tokens</span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Paper &amp; Ink</h2>
    <div class="sg-swatch-row">
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--paper)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--paper</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--paper2)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--paper2</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--body-bg)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--body-bg</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--ink)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--ink</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--ink2)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--ink2</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--ink3)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--ink3</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--rule-line)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--rule-line</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Accents</h2>
    <div class="sg-swatch-row">
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--green)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--green</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--green-bg)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--green-bg</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--blue)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--blue</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--blue-bg)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--blue-bg</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--orange)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--orange</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--orange-bg)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--orange-bg</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--red)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--red</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--purple)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--purple</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-swatch">
        <div class="sg-swatch-box" style="background:var(--yellow-hl)"></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch-name">--yellow-hl</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Spine Variants</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;position:relative;z-index:1;margin:8px 0 0">
      <div style="width:100px;height:48px;border-radius:2px 8px 8px 2px;box-shadow:-4px 0 0 var(--green),2px 2px 8px var(--shadow);background:var(--paper);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:13px;color:var(--green)">green-spine</div>
      <div style="width:100px;height:48px;border-radius:2px 8px 8px 2px;box-shadow:-4px 0 0 var(--blue),2px 2px 8px var(--shadow);background:var(--paper);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:13px;color:var(--blue)">blue-spine</div>
      <div style="width:100px;height:48px;border-radius:2px 8px 8px 2px;box-shadow:-4px 0 0 var(--orange),2px 2px 8px var(--shadow);background:var(--paper);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:13px;color:var(--orange)">orange-spine</div>
      <div style="width:100px;height:48px;border-radius:2px 8px 8px 2px;box-shadow:-4px 0 0 var(--purple),2px 2px 8px var(--shadow);background:var(--paper);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:13px;color:var(--purple)">purple-spine</div>
      <div style="width:100px;height:48px;border-radius:2px 8px 8px 2px;box-shadow:-4px 0 0 var(--red),2px 2px 8px var(--shadow);background:var(--paper);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:13px;color:var(--red)">red-spine</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Typography ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page green-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">✍️</span>
      <span class="section-title">Typography</span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Font Options</h2>
    <div style="position:relative;z-index:1;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px;margin-bottom:20px">
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="sg-font-sample" style="font-family:'Klee One',cursive">Klee One Aa Bb Cc<br />手書き風フォント</div>
        <div class="sg-font-label">--font-body default · data-font="klee"</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="sg-font-sample" style="font-family:'Gochi Hand',cursive">Gochi Hand Aa Bb<br />Headings &amp; labels</div>
        <div class="sg-font-label">--font-hand default · headings only</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="sg-font-sample" style="font-family:'Caveat',cursive">Caveat Aa Bb Cc<br />Casual scrawl</div>
        <div class="sg-font-label">data-font="caveat"</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="sg-font-sample" style="font-family:'Patrick Hand',cursive">Patrick Hand Aa Bb<br />Clean classroom</div>
        <div class="sg-font-label">data-font="patrick"</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="sg-font-sample" style="font-family:'Kalam',cursive">Kalam Aa Bb Cc<br />Warm notebook</div>
        <div class="sg-font-label">data-font="kalam"</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="sg-font-sample" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:18px">JetBrains Mono<br />const foo = 42;</div>
        <div class="sg-font-label">--font-mono · code only</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Text Styles</h2>
    <div class="body-text">
      <p>Body text uses <code>--font-body</code> at 18px, line-height 2.0 for comfortable reading.</p>
      <p>
        <span class="hl">Yellow highlight</span> ·
        <span class="hl-green">Green highlight</span> ·
        <span class="hl-blue">Blue highlight</span> ·
        <span class="hl-orange">Orange highlight</span> ·
        <span class="hl-purple">Purple highlight</span>
      </p>
      <p>
        <span class="wu">Wavy green underline</span> ·
        <span class="wu-o">Wavy orange underline</span> ·
        <span class="wu-b">Wavy blue underline</span>
      </p>
      <p>Inline <code>code</code> uses JetBrains Mono with a warm paper background.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Headings</h2>
    <h2 class="sub" style="margin-top:0">h2.sub — Section heading with dashed rule</h2>
    <h3 class="sub">h3.sub — Sub-section heading</h3>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Callouts ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page orange-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">📌</span>
      <span class="section-title">Callout Components</span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Sticky Notes</h2>
    <div class="sticky">
      <div class="sticky-label">📌 Default Sticky</div>
      <p>A <strong>yellow sticky note</strong> for key takeaways, mental models, or reminders. Slightly rotated for a hand-placed feel.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sticky" style="transform:rotate(0.5deg)">
      <div class="sticky-label">⭐ Variation</div>
      <p>Use a positive rotation for variety when multiple stickies appear on one page.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Insight Boxes</h2>
    <div class="insight">
      <div class="insight-label">💡 Default — Blue</div>
      <p>General insights, references, or important clarifications. Uses <code>--blue</code> left border.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight green-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">✅ Green Variant</div>
      <p>Use for positive findings, best practices, or things that work well.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight orange-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">⚡ Orange Variant</div>
      <p>Use for pro tips, performance notes, or things worth paying extra attention to.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Code ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page purple-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">💻</span>
      <span class="section-title">Code Blocks</span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Default (blue left border)</h2>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="an">@Service</span>
<span class="kw">public class</span> <span class="cl">UserService</span> &#123;
  <span class="kw">private final</span> <span class="cl">UserRepository</span> repo;

  <span class="cm">// Constructor injection — preferred</span>
  <span class="kw">public</span> UserService(<span class="cl">UserRepository</span> repo) &#123;
    <span class="kw">this</span>.repo = repo;
  &#125;

  <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cl">User</span> findById(<span class="cl">Long</span> id) &#123;
    <span class="kw">return</span> repo.findById(id)
      .orElseThrow(() <span class="ar">-&gt;</span> <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="cl">NotFoundException</span>(id));
  &#125;
&#125;</pre>

    <h2 class="sub">Accent Variants</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="body-text" style="font-size:14px;margin-bottom:4px"><code>.green-left</code></div>
        <pre class="code-block green-left"><span class="cm">// Success path</span>
<span class="kw">return</span> <span class="cl">ResponseEntity</span>.ok(result);</pre>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="body-text" style="font-size:14px;margin-bottom:4px"><code>.orange-left</code></div>
        <pre class="code-block orange-left"><span class="cm">// Warning / legacy</span>
<span class="an">@Deprecated</span>
<span class="kw">public void</span> oldMethod() &#123;&#125;</pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Syntax Token Classes</h2>
    <table class="note-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Use for</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>.kw</code></td><td>Keywords</td><td><span class="hl-blue" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px">public, class, return</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>.an</code></td><td>Annotations</td><td><span class="hl-green" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px">@Service, @Bean</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>.cl</code></td><td>Class names</td><td><span class="hl-purple" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px">UserService</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>.st</code></td><td>Strings</td><td><span class="hl-orange" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px">"singleton"</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>.cm</code></td><td>Comments</td><td><span style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;color:#7a8a6a">// comment</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>.ar</code></td><td>Arrows / operators</td><td><span style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;color:var(--orange);font-weight:500">→ , -&gt;</span></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Diagrams ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page green-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">📊</span>
      <span class="section-title">Diagram Patterns</span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Horizontal Flow</h2>
    <div class="diag-wrap">
      <div class="flow-row">
        <div class="flow-box fb-gray">Input<br /><span style="font-size:11px;opacity:0.7">raw data</span></div>
        <div class="flow-arr">→</div>
        <div class="flow-box fb-blue">Process<br /><span style="font-size:11px;opacity:0.7">transform</span></div>
        <div class="flow-arr">→</div>
        <div class="flow-box fb-green">Output<br /><span style="font-size:11px;opacity:0.7">result</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="body-text"><p>Use <code>.flow-row</code> + <code>.flow-box.fb-*</code> + <code>.flow-arr</code>. Available colors: <code>fb-gray</code>, <code>fb-blue</code>, <code>fb-green</code>, <code>fb-purple</code>, <code>fb-orange</code>.</p></div>

    <h2 class="sub">Vertical Phase Flow</h2>
    <div class="diag-wrap">
      <div class="phase-flow">
        <div class="phase-box ph-blue">
          <div class="ph-num">Phase 1</div>
          <div class="ph-title">🔵 First Step</div>
          <div class="ph-sub">Description of what happens here</div>
        </div>
        <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="phase-box ph-green">
          <div class="ph-num">Phase 2</div>
          <div class="ph-title">🟢 Second Step</div>
          <div class="ph-sub">Description of what happens here</div>
        </div>
        <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="phase-box ph-orange">
          <div class="ph-num">Phase 3</div>
          <div class="ph-title">🟠 Final Step</div>
          <div class="ph-sub">End result or outcome</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="body-text"><p>Use <code>.phase-flow</code> + <code>.phase-box.ph-*</code> + <code>.phase-arrow</code>. Available: <code>ph-gray</code>, <code>ph-blue</code>, <code>ph-green</code>, <code>ph-orange</code>, <code>ph-purple</code>, <code>ph-red</code>.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Lists & Tables ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page red-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">📋</span>
      <span class="section-title">Lists &amp; Tables</span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Note List Variants</h2>
    <ul class="note-list">
      <li>Default arrow bullet (→) — for general items</li>
      <li class="sq">Square bullet (▸) — for secondary / nested info</li>
      <li class="ck">Check bullet (✓) — for pros / advantages</li>
      <li class="cr">Cross bullet (✗) — for cons / avoid</li>
      <li class="st">Star bullet (★) — for highlights / key points</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="sub">Note Table</h2>
    <div class="body-text">
      <p>A self-contained <span class="hl-green">paper card</span> — opaque cells (no page-line bleed-through), subtle outer ring, soft drop shadow, alternating row tint, and clear column dividers. Theme-safe via <code>--paper</code> / <code>--paper2</code>. Scrolls horizontally on mobile automatically.</p>
    </div>
    <table class="note-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Column A</th><th>Column B</th><th>Column C</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Row 1 A</td><td>Row 1 B</td><td>Row 1 C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Row 2 A</td><td>Row 2 B</td><td>Row 2 C</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Row 3 A</td><td>Row 3 B</td><td>Row 3 C</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 class="sub">Use case — concurrency timeline</h3>
    <div class="body-text">
      <p>For time-series or two-actor timelines, use a 3-column table with a narrow <code>Time</code> anchor column. Empty cells read as "idle"; <code>&lt;code&gt;</code> wraps SQL keywords; <code>.hl-green</code> / <code>.hl-orange</code> mark correct vs. anomalous values.</p>
    </div>
    <table class="note-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th style="width:60px">Time</th><th>Transaction A</th><th>Transaction B</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>T1</strong></td><td><code>BEGIN</code></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>T2</strong></td><td><code>UPDATE</code> balance = 500 <em>(uncommitted)</em></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>T3</strong></td><td></td><td><code>SELECT</code> balance → <span class="hl-orange">500</span> ❌ <strong>dirty!</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>T4</strong></td><td><code>ROLLBACK</code></td><td></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="insight orange-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">⚠️ Don't draw tables with ASCII art</div>
      <p>Never use <code>│ ─ ┼ ┌ └</code> characters inside <code>&lt;pre class="code-block"&gt;</code> to draw a table. Use real <code>&lt;table class="note-table"&gt;</code> markup — the page's lined-paper texture leaks through code blocks and turns ASCII tables into visual noise.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Two-Column Cards</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="col-card-title g">✅ Green Title</div>
        <div class="body-text" style="font-size:14px;margin:0">Use for benefits, the "good" side, or recommended approach.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="col-card-title r">❌ Red Title</div>
        <div class="body-text" style="font-size:14px;margin:0">Use for drawbacks, the "bad" side, or anti-patterns.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Cheat grid ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page orange-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">📝</span>
      <span class="section-title">Cheat Grid</span>
    </div>
    <div class="body-text"><p>Use <code>.cheat-grid</code> + <code>.cheat-card</code> for quick reference sections at the end of a note. Set <code>color</code> and <code>border-top-color</code> on each card to the appropriate accent variable.</p></div>
    <div class="cheat-grid">
      <div class="cheat-card" style="color:var(--green);border-top-color:var(--green)">
        <div class="cheat-card-title">🟢 Green Card</div>
        <pre class="code-block" style="margin:0;font-size:12px;border-left-color:var(--green)"><span class="an">@Component</span>
<span class="an">@Service</span></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="cheat-card" style="color:var(--blue);border-top-color:var(--blue)">
        <div class="cheat-card-title">🔵 Blue Card</div>
        <pre class="code-block" style="margin:0;font-size:12px;border-left-color:var(--blue)"><span class="an">@Autowired</span>
<span class="an">@Qualifier</span></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="cheat-card" style="color:var(--orange);border-top-color:var(--orange)">
        <div class="cheat-card-title">🟠 Orange Card</div>
        <pre class="code-block" style="margin:0;font-size:12px;border-left-color:var(--orange)"><span class="an">@Scope</span>(<span class="st">"prototype"</span>)</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="cheat-card" style="color:var(--purple);border-top-color:var(--purple)">
        <div class="cheat-card-title">🟣 Purple Card</div>
        <pre class="code-block" style="margin:0;font-size:12px;border-left-color:var(--purple)"><span class="an">@PostConstruct</span>
<span class="an">@PreDestroy</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── Mobile & Responsive ── -->
<div class="sg-section">
  <div class="page green-spine">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-icon">📱</span>
      <span class="section-title">Mobile &amp; Responsive</span>
    </div>

    <div class="body-text">
      <p>All responsive rules live in the <span class="hl-green">Responsive</span> section at the bottom of <code>components.css</code>. Three breakpoints cover tablet, phone, and small phone.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Breakpoints</h2>
    <table class="note-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Breakpoint</th><th>Target</th><th>Key changes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>≤ 768px</code></td>
          <td>Tablet</td>
          <td>Tighter card padding, smaller cover h1 (28px), decorative section-num shrinks</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>≤ 640px</code></td>
          <td>Phone</td>
          <td>Single-column grids, font sizes reduced, <code>.page-num</code> hidden, cover compact, sticky rotation off</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>≤ 480px</code></td>
          <td>Small phone</td>
          <td>Further size reduction, cover-subject hidden, pagination title hidden, nav tightened</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="sub">Rules for new components</h2>
    <ul class="note-list">
      <li>Never use hard pixel widths on layout containers — use <code>max-width</code> + <code>width: 100%</code></li>
      <li class="sq">New <span class="hl-blue">multi-column grids</span> must be added to the <code>≤ 640px</code> block with <code>grid-template-columns: 1fr</code></li>
      <li class="sq">New <span class="hl-blue">tables</span> must get <code>display: block; overflow-x: auto</code> at <code>≤ 640px</code> — the <code>.note-table</code> rule is the reference</li>
      <li class="sq">New <span class="hl-blue">code blocks</span> scroll horizontally automatically — <code>overflow-x: auto</code> + <code>white-space: pre</code> handle it</li>
      <li class="sq">New <span class="hl-orange">decorative-only elements</span> (doodles, background numbers, hints) must be hidden at <code>≤ 640px</code> or <code>≤ 480px</code></li>
      <li class="sq">New <span class="hl-orange">fixed elements</span> must check positioning under <code>body.pg-mode</code> (pagination bar active)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="sub">Known mobile fixes (do not remove)</h2>

    <div class="insight orange-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">⚠️ .page-num hidden at ≤ 640px</div>
      <p>The "pg 01" badge is <code>position: absolute; top: 16px; right: 24px</code>. At reduced page padding it overlaps the section header. The pagination bar already shows the current page — hiding the badge on mobile removes the overlap without losing information.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="insight green-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">✅ .section-title has flex: 1; min-width: 0</div>
      <p>This is a global rule (not mobile-only). It allows long section titles to wrap inside the flex row instead of overflowing. Any new flex-row text element needs the same treatment.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="insight">
      <div class="insight-label">💡 .sticky transform: none at ≤ 640px</div>
      <p>The <code>rotate(-0.4deg)</code> decoration clips against card edges on narrow screens. Mobile sticky notes are flat — the warmth comes from the yellow background alone.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">What scales automatically (no extra work needed)</h2>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="col-card-title g">✓ Handled by CSS</div>
        <ul class="note-list" style="margin:0">
          <li class="ck">Code blocks scroll horizontally</li>
          <li class="ck">Diagram wrappers scroll horizontally</li>
          <li class="ck"><code>.two-col</code> stacks to 1 column</li>
          <li class="ck"><code>.cheat-grid</code> stacks to 1 column</li>
          <li class="ck">Flow diagrams go vertical</li>
          <li class="ck">Tags wrap to new lines</li>
          <li class="ck">Cover shrinks compactly</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col-card">
        <div class="col-card-title r">✗ You must handle manually</div>
        <ul class="note-list" style="margin:0">
          <li class="cr">New 2-col grids (add 1fr override)</li>
          <li class="cr">New tables (add overflow-x rule)</li>
          <li class="cr">New fixed elements (check pg-mode offset)</li>
          <li class="cr">Hard-coded pixel widths</li>
          <li class="cr">Decorative-only elements (hide them)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="sub">Swipe navigation &amp; scrollable elements</h2>
    <div class="body-text">
      <p>The <code>PaginationController</code> listens for horizontal swipe gestures on the whole page to navigate between note pages. This conflicts with <span class="hl-orange">horizontally scrollable elements</span> such as code blocks and diagram wrappers — a user trying to scroll code would accidentally navigate to the next page instead.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight orange-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">⚠️ Swipe conflict — already fixed, keep this pattern</div>
      <p>On every <code>touchstart</code>, the controller records the target element. On <code>touchend</code>, it walks up the DOM tree checking for any ancestor with <code>overflow-x: auto | scroll</code> <em>and</em> <code>scrollWidth &gt; clientWidth</code> (meaning the element actually has overflowing content). If one is found, the swipe is treated as a scroll gesture and page navigation is skipped entirely.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight green-ins">
      <div class="insight-label">✅ Rule — any new scrollable element gets this for free</div>
      <p>The check is DOM-walk based, not class-based. Any element you add with <code>overflow-x: auto</code> or <code>overflow-x: scroll</code> that has wider content than its container will automatically be protected from swipe-nav conflict. No extra code needed.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="note-list">
      <li class="ck">Code blocks (<code>.code-block</code>) — protected automatically</li>
      <li class="ck">Diagram wrappers (<code>.diag-wrap</code>) — protected automatically</li>
      <li class="ck">Tables on mobile (<code>.note-table</code> with <code>overflow-x: auto</code>) — protected automatically</li>
      <li class="cr">Never add swipe navigation outside <code>PaginationController</code> — duplicate listeners cause double-navigate bugs</li>
      <li class="cr">Never remove the <code>isInsideHScrollable</code> guard from <code>PaginationController.astro</code></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="sticky" style="margin-top:20px">
      <div class="sticky-label">📐 Test on real devices</div>
      <p>Always resize the browser to <strong>360px</strong> (common Android), <strong>390px</strong> (iPhone 14), and <strong>768px</strong> (iPad) when building new pages. The responsive rules were tuned for these widths.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</BaseLayout>
